From 7302ad482d221e7a4f25740d99b08e63efbe96cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 23rd <23rd@vivaldi.net>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 17:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Ported Windows 7 backport from Qt 6.10.0 to Qt 6.11.1.

Three-way merged all 39 overlay files against pristine qtbase v6.10.0
and v6.11.1. Notes on the parts that were not mechanical:

- qwindowstheme.cpp: Qt 6.11 restructured qt_accentColor() into "try
  WinRT, fall back to the DWM registry key", which is what the backport
  did by hand. Kept upstream's shape and only added the
  IsWindows10OrGreater() gate so WinRT UISettings is never activated on
  Windows 7/8.1. The Win7 delta here shrank from 80 to 15 lines.
- qwindowscontext.cpp: Qt 6.11 moved window class registration into the
  new qwindowswindowclassregistry, so only the dynamic user32/shcore
  symbol resolution and the QLegacyShims fallbacks remain.
- qeventdispatcher_win.cpp: moved the dynamic SetCoalescableTimer lookup
  inside the existing "if (!ok)" block so tdesktop's stock
  0008-fix-race-in-windows-timers.patch applies without local edits.

Verified the new Qt 6.11 code stays Win7-safe: qatomicwait falls back to
its mutex implementation because the backport disables QtFutex on
Windows, and qioring_win resolves every IoRing entry point through
GetProcAddress.
